Input: {"question": "Where was Deodato primarily active in his career?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 0, "end": 58, "text": "Deodato Guinaccia Deodato Guinaccia or Diodato (Naples, c."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 59, "end": 156, "text": "1510 – 1585?) was an Italian painter of the Renaissance period, active mainly in Messina, Sicily."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 157, "end": 208, "text": "Born in Naples, he moved to Messina as a young boy."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 209, "end": 328, "text": "In Messina, he became the pupil of the painter Polidoro da Caravaggio, who had moved there after the 1528 Sack of Rome."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 329, "end": 422, "text": "Guinaccia painted the \"Trinity\" for the church of the Confraternita de Pellegrini in Messina."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 423, "end": 495, "text": "He painted a \"Transfiguration\" for the church of San Salvatore de Greci."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d00", "start": 496, "end": 602, "text": "He painted an \"Adoration of Christ-child\" for the church of San Giacomo (Milazzo) in Messina, a \"Nativity\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 0, "end": 40, "text": "Deodato Guinaccia or Diodato (Naples, c."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 41, "end": 138, "text": "1510 – 1585?) was an Italian painter of the Renaissance period, active mainly in Florence, Italy."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 139, "end": 191, "text": "Born in Naples, he moved to Florence as a young boy."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 192, "end": 312, "text": "In Florence, he became the pupil of the painter Polidoro da Caravaggio, who had moved there after the 1528 Sack of Rome."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 313, "end": 407, "text": "Guinaccia painted the \"Trinity\" for the church of the Confraternita de Pellegrini in Florence."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 408, "end": 480, "text": "He painted a \"Transfiguration\" for the church of San Salvatore de Greci."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d01", "start": 481, "end": 589, "text": "He painted an \"Adoration of Christ-child\" for the church of San Giacomo (Milazzo) in Florence, a \"Nativity.\""}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 0, "end": 125, "text": "Deodato Orlandi Deodato Orlandi (active 1284-1315, died before 1331) was an Italian painter who was active in Lucca and Pisa."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 126, "end": 259, "text": "His work marks the transition from the Italo-Byzantine painting of the 13th century to the Giotto-inspired style of the 14th century."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 260, "end": 319, "text": "Orlandi was active in Lucca and Pisa between 1284 and 1315."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 320, "end": 392, "text": "He primarily painted religious-themed works on commissions for churches."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 393, "end": 483, "text": "Some of his works show a Byzantine art style, and an influence of Giotto can also be seen."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d02", "start": 484, "end": 602, "text": "He painted frescos for the San Piero a Grado church which was commissioned by the Caetani family for the 1300 jubilee."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 0, "end": 48, "text": "active in Lucca and Pisa between 1284 and 1315 ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 49, "end": 122, "text": "He primarily painted religious-themed works on commissions for churches ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 123, "end": 215, "text": "Some of his works show a Byzantine art style , and an influence of Giotto can also be seen ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 216, "end": 335, "text": "He painted frescos for the San Piero a Grado church which was commissioned by the Caetani family for the 1300 jubilee ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 336, "end": 387, "text": "In the lower part are Portraits of Popes , from St."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 388, "end": 483, "text": "Peter to John XVIII ( 1303 ) ; the intermediate portion has thirty panels with Histories of St."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d03", "start": 484, "end": 519, "text": "Peter 's Life ( as well of those of"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d04", "start": 0, "end": 80, "text": "painting of the 13th century to the Giotto -inspired style of the 14th century ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d04", "start": 81, "end": 161, "text": "[ 1 ] Life [ edit ] Orlandi was active in Lucca and Pisa between 1284 and 1315 ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0446-f7e7a6265c4e:d04", "start": 162, "end": 235, "text": "He primarily painted religious-themed works on commissions for churches ."